-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 121 to 147 -- WORKED CASES FOR THE SEAT LAYER (dg2-seat.l4).
--
-- One or more cases per question, each stated as the person in the seat would state the facts. The expected answer is written beside each
-- case from the text of the section the question cites, before the run; a question whose rule says NOTHING where the text does not say
-- has a case asserting NOTHING. The cases call the questions (the thin layer), not the layer-1 rules: the rules are tested in the dg2-tests-* files.


§§ `Powers (ss 121 to 127)`
-- #1 A stockholder: the Law grants the power and it serves our purposes.
#ASSERT `Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #1 The certificate grants it but it does not serve our purposes: the "so far as" limit is not met.
#ASSERT `Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #1 Nothing grants it and it is not incidental, though it would serve us.
#ASSERT `Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #1 Incidental to a granted power and necessary or convenient.
#ASSERT `Do my corporation, its officers, directors and stockholders possess and may they exercise this power` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #2 An incorporator: the corporation is organized under the chapter.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation governed by the General Corporation Law and subject to its restrictions and liabilities` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #2 Not organized under the chapter: the subsection does not say.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation governed by the General Corporation Law and subject to its restrictions and liabilities` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #3 Perpetual succession; the certificate states no limited duration.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to have perpetual succession by its corporate name, under s 122(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Perpetual succession; the certificate states a limited period of duration.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to have perpetual succession by its corporate name, under s 122(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #3 The power to sue and be sued needs no fact beyond creation under the chapter.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to sue and be sued in all courts and to participate in any proceeding in its corporate name, under s 122(2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Participating in a transaction we could not conduct by ourselves.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to participate with others in an association of any kind, or in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement, under s 122(11)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #3 Participating in a transaction we could conduct by ourselves.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to participate with others in an association of any kind, or in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement, under s 122(11)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Participating in an association of any kind.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to participate with others in an association of any kind, or in a transaction, undertaking or arrangement, under s 122(11)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Lawful business that the board finds to be in aid of governmental authority.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to transact any lawful business which the corporation's board of directors finds to be in aid of governmental authority, under s 122(12)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Lawful business, but the board has made no such finding.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to transact any lawful business which the corporation's board of directors finds to be in aid of governmental authority, under s 122(12)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #3 Lending for our corporate purposes.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to lend money for its corporate purposes, under s 122(14)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Insurance for our benefit on the life of a stockholder, to acquire the stockholder's shares at death.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to provide insurance for its benefit on the life of a director, officer, employee or stockholder, under s 122(16)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the life of a stockholder of the corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #3 Insurance on the life of a stockholder not for acquiring the shares.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to provide insurance for its benefit on the life of a director, officer, employee or stockholder, under s 122(16)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `the life of a stockholder of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #3 Insurance on the life of an employee, not for our benefit.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to provide insurance for its benefit on the life of a director, officer, employee or stockholder, under s 122(16)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #3 Not created under the chapter: the paragraph does not speak.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have this specific power` `to sue and be sued in all courts and to participate in any proceeding in its corporate name, under s 122(2)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `the life of a director, officer or employee of the corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #4 A delegation of authority to an officer or agent is subject to section 141(a).
#ASSERT `Is a contract or delegation that empowers an officer or agent to act for my corporation subject to the board's management power` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #4 No delegation: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is a contract or delegation that empowers an officer or agent to act for my corporation subject to the board's management power` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #5 A guaranty for our wholly owned subsidiary is deemed necessary or convenient, whatever the facts.
#ASSERT `Is a guaranty my corporation gives for another company within its power as necessary or convenient to its business` `a corporation all of the outstanding stock of which is owned, directly or indirectly, by the contracting corporation` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #5 A guaranty for an unrelated company that is in fact necessary or convenient.
#ASSERT `Is a guaranty my corporation gives for another company within its power as necessary or convenient to its business` `a person or entity in some other relationship to the contracting corporation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #5 A guaranty for an unrelated company not shown necessary or convenient: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is a guaranty my corporation gives for another company within its power as necessary or convenient to its business` `a person or entity in some other relationship to the contracting corporation` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #6 Renounced in the certificate: specified opportunities presented to us.
#ASSERT `May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities` `in the certificate of incorporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #6 Renounced by a resolution of the board.
#ASSERT `May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities` `in a resolution of the board of directors` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #6 Renounced in the bylaws: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities` `in the bylaws` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #6 A blanket renunciation, not of specified opportunities: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation renounce an interest or expectancy in business opportunities` `in the certificate of incorporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #7 A contract with current stockholders as such, for the consideration the board set.
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this contract with stockholders` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #7 The consideration is below the board's minimum.
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this contract with stockholders` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #7 A contract with someone who is not a stockholder in that capacity.
#ASSERT `May my corporation make this contract with stockholders` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #8 A provision contrary to nothing: enforceable.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #8 A provision contrary to the certificate: not enforceable against the corporation.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #8 A provision that would be contrary to the laws if put in the certificate.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #8 A covenant on a specified action, contrary only because a provision authorizes the board to take that action: deemed not contrary.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #8 A covenant on a specified action, but contrary for another reason too.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #8 Not a contract under paragraph (18): the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Can I enforce this provision of my contract with the corporation against it, as a stockholder` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #9 An undertaking to restrict itself from specified actions.
#ASSERT `May my corporation agree to this kind of undertaking in a contract with stockholders` `to restrict or prohibit itself from taking actions specified in the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #9 A covenant that persons will take or refrain from taking actions.
#ASSERT `May my corporation agree to this kind of undertaking in a contract with stockholders` `to covenant that it or 1 or more persons or bodies will take, or refrain from taking, actions specified in the contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #9 An undertaking of any other kind: the list does not limit, and the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation agree to this kind of undertaking in a contract with stockholders` `an undertaking of any other kind` EQUALS NOTHING
-- #10 Subject to the remedies of the governing law if we fail to perform.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation subject to the remedies of the law governing a contract it made with stockholders, if it fails to perform` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #10 Not a paragraph (18) contract: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation subject to the remedies of the law governing a contract it made with stockholders, if it fails to perform` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #11 A Delaware corporation holding shares of another corporation.
#ASSERT `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` TRUE `to own, hold, use or otherwise employ` `another domestic or foreign corporation, under s 123` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #11 Bonds of a government.
#ASSERT `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` TRUE `to mortgage, lend, pledge or otherwise deal in and with` `a government or an agency or instrumentality of a government, under s 123` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #11 Interests in an issuer of some other kind: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` TRUE `to own, hold, use or otherwise employ` `an issuer of some other kind, under s 123` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #11 Not securities of the issuer: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` TRUE `to own, hold, use or otherwise employ` `a partnership, under s 123` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #11 A corporation not organized under Delaware law: the section does not speak.
#ASSERT `May my corporation deal in the securities of another entity in this way` FALSE `to own, hold, use or otherwise employ` `an individual, under s 123` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #12 We own the securities, so we may vote them.
#ASSERT `May my corporation vote the securities of another entity that it owns, and exercise the other rights of ownership` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #12 We do not own them: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May my corporation vote the securities of another entity that it owns, and exercise the other rights of ownership` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #13 An act beyond our power is not invalid for that reason.
#ASSERT `Is an act of my corporation, or a conveyance to or by it, invalid because my corporation lacked the capacity or power` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #13 An act within our power is not invalid for that reason either.
#ASSERT `Is an act of my corporation, or a conveyance to or by it, invalid because my corporation lacked the capacity or power` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #14 A stockholder sues the corporation to enjoin an act.
#ASSERT `Can the corporation's lack of capacity or power be asserted in this proceeding` `a proceeding by a stockholder against the corporation to enjoin the doing of an act or the transfer of property by or to the corporation` EQUALS TRUE
-- #14 The Attorney General sues to dissolve the corporation.
#ASSERT `Can the corporation's lack of capacity or power be asserted in this proceeding` `a proceeding by the Attorney General to dissolve the corporation, or to enjoin the corporation from the transaction of unauthorized business` EQUALS TRUE
-- #14 A proceeding of any other kind: the lack of power may not be asserted.
#ASSERT `Can the corporation's lack of capacity or power be asserted in this proceeding` `a proceeding of any other kind` EQUALS FALSE
-- #15 All parties are in the proceeding and the court finds it equitable.
#ASSERT `May the court set aside and enjoin the performance of a contract of my corporation in a stockholder's suit to enjoin an unauthorized act` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #15 A party to the contract is missing from the proceeding.
#ASSERT `May the court set aside and enjoin the performance of a contract of my corporation in a stockholder's suit to enjoin an unauthorized act` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #15 The court does not find it equitable.
#ASSERT `May the court set aside and enjoin the performance of a contract of my corporation in a stockholder's suit to enjoin an unauthorized act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #16 An anticipated profit may not be awarded as a loss.
#ASSERT `May the court award an anticipated profit as a loss or damage sustained when it sets a contract aside` TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #16 A loss that is not an anticipated profit may be.
#ASSERT `May the court award an anticipated profit as a loss or damage sustained when it sets a contract aside` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #17 The court set the contract aside: it may allow equitable compensation.
#ASSERT `May the court allow compensation to my corporation or the other parties for loss from setting the contract aside` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #17 The court did not: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May the court allow compensation to my corporation or the other parties for loss from setting the contract aside` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #18 Organized in 1960; certificate provides for degrees and carries the Department's approval.
#ASSERT `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` (YMD 1960 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #18 Organized in 1960; the certificate provides for degrees but lacks the Department's approval.
#ASSERT `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` (YMD 1960 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #18 Organized in 1930; amendment filed with the Department's approval endorsed.
#ASSERT `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` (YMD 1930 1 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #18 Organized in 1930; amendment filed without the approval.
#ASSERT `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` (YMD 1930 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #18 Organized exactly on April 18, 1945: the text names neither side.
#ASSERT `May my corporation confer academic or honorary degrees` (YMD 1945 4 18) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #19 Neither a bona fide institution nor a good-faith proposal appears: no approval may be granted.
#ASSERT `Is the Department of Education allowed to approve my corporation's power to confer degrees` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #19 One of them appears: the text does not say that the Department must or need not.
#ASSERT `Is the Department of Education allowed to approve my corporation's power to confer degrees` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #20 We confer degrees and are dissolving.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation comply with section 8530 of Title 14 when it dissolves` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #20 We are not dissolving: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation comply with section 8530 of Title 14 when it dissolves` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #21 The certificate carries the Department's approval under Chapter 85 of Title 14.
#ASSERT `May my corporation conduct a private business or trade school` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #21 It does not.
#ASSERT `May my corporation conduct a private business or trade school` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #22 All conditions met; the dean was retained exactly one year after operation began.
#ASSERT `Does my law school corporation have temporary approval from the State` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 9 1) (YMD 2021 9 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #22 The dean was retained one day short of a year.
#ASSERT `Does my law school corporation have temporary approval from the State` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 9 1) (YMD 2021 8 31) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #22 We filed no copy of the report.
#ASSERT `Does my law school corporation have temporary approval from the State` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2020 9 1) (YMD 2022 1 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #23 Temporary approval, ABA approval not yet given: a new report is due.
#ASSERT `Must my law school corporation file a new report this academic year` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #23 The ABA has approved the school: no new report.
#ASSERT `Must my law school corporation file a new report this academic year` TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #24 We failed to file the report and the Secretary of Education asked.
#ASSERT `Can the Attorney General sue in the Court of Chancery to suspend my law school corporation's temporary approval and degree-granting power` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #24 The Secretary of Education has not asked.
#ASSERT `Can the Attorney General sue in the Court of Chancery to suspend my law school corporation's temporary approval and degree-granting power` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #24 The ABA has approved the school.
#ASSERT `Can the Attorney General sue in the Court of Chancery to suspend my law school corporation's temporary approval and degree-granting power` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #25 The ABA has approved the school: approval is final.
#ASSERT `Has my law school corporation's temporary approval become final and no longer subject to suspension` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #25 It has not.
#ASSERT `Has my law school corporation's temporary approval become final and no longer subject to suspension` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #26 The power to receive deposits of money is denied.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the power to issue money-like notes or to take deposits` TRUE `carrying on the business of receiving deposits of money` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #26 The power to issue notes for circulation as money is denied.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the power to issue money-like notes or to take deposits` TRUE `issuing bills, notes, or other evidences of debt for circulation as money` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #26 Any other activity: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `Does my corporation have the power to issue money-like notes or to take deposits` TRUE `any other activity` EQUALS NOTHING
-- #27 Organized to deal in notes: not banking.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation engaging in the business of banking because it deals in notes or lends against collateral` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #27 Organized for neither: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation engaging in the business of banking because it deals in notes or lends against collateral` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #28 A Delaware private foundation whose certificate does not opt out: self-dealing tax.
#ASSERT `Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax` TRUE TRUE FALSE `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4941 (taxes on self-dealing)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #28 The certificate expressly opts out of section 127.
#ASSERT `Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4941 (taxes on self-dealing)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #28 Not a private foundation.
#ASSERT `Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the tax imposed by 26 U.S.C. section 4941 (taxes on self-dealing)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #28 A tax of any other kind: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `Must my private foundation act or refrain from acting so as not to incur this federal tax` TRUE TRUE FALSE `a tax of any other kind` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `The registered office and the registered agent (ss 131 to 136)`
-- #29 An incorporator: the corporation is organized under the chapter.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation have and maintain a registered office in Delaware` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #29 Not organized under the chapter: the subsection does not say.
#ASSERT `Must my corporation have and maintain a registered office in Delaware` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #30 Our registered office is at a place where we do business in Delaware.
#ASSERT `May my registered office be at a place where my corporation does business in Delaware` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #30 It is not a place of our business: still allowed.
#ASSERT `May my registered office be at a place where my corporation does business in Delaware` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #31 Our agent's address is in Delaware.
#ASSERT `What is my corporation's registered office` "100 West Street, Wilmington, DE" TRUE EQUALS JUST "100 West Street, Wilmington, DE"
-- #31 Our agent's address is outside Delaware: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `What is my corporation's registered office` "1 Elm Street, Camden, NJ" FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #32 An address with the street, number, city, county and postal code.
#ASSERT `Is the address of my registered office, as it appears in a document filed with the Secretary of State, complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #32 An address that leaves out the county.
#ASSERT `Is the address of my registered office, as it appears in a document filed with the Secretary of State, complete` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #33 An individual resident in Delaware.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `an individual, as a candidate for registered agent` `this State` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #33 An individual not resident in Delaware.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `an individual, as a candidate for registered agent` `this State` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #33 A foreign corporation.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `a corporation, as a candidate for registered agent` `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #33 A domestic general partnership.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `a general partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` `this State` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #33 A foreign general partnership that is not a limited liability partnership: not in the list.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `a general partnership, as a candidate for registered agent` `another jurisdiction of the United States` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #33 A limited liability company.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `a limited liability company, as a candidate for registered agent` `another jurisdiction of the United States` FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #33 A real estate investment trust: in neither list.
#ASSERT `May this person or entity be my corporation's registered agent` `a business trust, real estate investment trust, common-law trust, joint-stock association or any other unincorporated business, as a candidate for registered agent` `this State` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #34 An entity agent with a generally open Delaware office that forwards everything and follows the Secretary's regulations.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #34 An individual agent generally present at a designated location.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #34 An entity agent whose office is not generally open.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #34 A foreign entity agent not authorized to transact business here.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #34 An agent that does not forward the annual report.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent doing what the Law requires of every registered agent` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #35 An agent working solely through a virtual office.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #35 An agent using a mail forwarding service and also working in person.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #35 An agent using a mail forwarding service and nothing else.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #35 An agent that does neither.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent perform its duties in this way` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #36 An agent that serves 51 entities at one time: more than 50.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` 51 FALSE 0 EQUALS TRUE
-- #36 An agent that serves exactly 50 entities: not more than 50.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` 50 FALSE 0 EQUALS FALSE
-- #36 An agent sharing an officer with another agent, together serving 51.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` 30 TRUE 51 EQUALS TRUE
-- #36 An agent sharing an officer with another agent, together serving exactly 50.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` 30 TRUE 50 EQUALS FALSE
-- #36 The shared count does not matter without a shared officer.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent a commercial registered agent` 30 FALSE 99 EQUALS FALSE
-- #37 A commercial agent that is a natural person with every qualification.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent` 60 FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #37 A commercial agent that is an entity with every qualification.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent` 60 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- #37 A commercial agent that is an entity without a Delaware business license.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent` 60 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- #37 An agent that is not commercial need not meet the qualifications.
#ASSERT `Is my corporation's registered agent in compliance with the qualifications for a commercial registered agent` 10 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #38 We gave the agent the name, address and telephone number of an authorized officer, and keep it current.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation given its registered agent the communications contact the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #38 We never gave the agent a telephone number.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation given its registered agent the communications contact the Law requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #38 We are neither formed nor qualified in Delaware: not covered.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation given its registered agent the communications contact the Law requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #39 The agent keeps the information on paper.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation's registered agent kept the information about our communications contact as the Law requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #39 The agent keeps it in neither form.
#ASSERT `Has my corporation's registered agent kept the information about our communications contact as the Law requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #40 We gave no current contact: the agent may resign.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent resign because we have not given it a current communications contact` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #40 We did give one: the text does not say the agent may resign on this ground.
#ASSERT `May my corporation's registered agent resign because we have not given it a current communications contact` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #41 The Secretary refuses a document my agent submitted, as reasonable and necessary to assure compliance.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State refuse to file a document that my registered agent submitted` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #41 The refusal is not shown reasonable and necessary: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May the Secretary of State refuse to file a document that my registered agent submitted` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #42 The Secretary has not applied: the Court may not enjoin under this section.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery enjoin a person or entity from serving as a registered agent, or as an officer, director or managing agent of one` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- #42 The Secretary applied and a ground exists.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery enjoin a person or entity from serving as a registered agent, or as an officer, director or managing agent of one` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #42 The Secretary applied but no ground exists: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery enjoin a person or entity from serving as a registered agent, or as an officer, director or managing agent of one` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #43 The Secretary has filed a complaint: the Court may make orders, interim or final.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery make orders, including interim or final relief, in the Secretary's proceeding against my registered agent or its officers` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- #43 The Secretary has filed no complaint: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `May the Court of Chancery make orders, including interim or final relief, in the Secretary's proceeding against my registered agent or its officers` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- #44 Commercial within the year (on the complaint date minus one year) and failed after a warning.
#ASSERT `Is there a ground on which the Court of Chancery may be asked to enjoin my registered agent or its officers` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- #44 Last commercial one day before the one-year window opened.
#ASSERT `Is there a ground on which the Court of Chancery may be asked to enjoin my registered agent or its officers` TRUE (YMD 2025 5 31) (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- #44 Not commercial within the year, though it failed after a warning.
